      "evidence": "template/scripts/lifecycle_workers.py:1589-1592 posts `result_body(job, worker, 'waiting-required-checks')`. `job_completed` (lifecycle_workers.py:317-320) returns True for any outcome that is not validated-push, discarded*, unavailable* or released*, so the job is never re-offered. Previously the ContributionError failed the run and `release_claim` retried it up to MAX_RELEASES. The queue path at publication_queue.py:2382-2390 does re-run `merge_reviewed_contribution`, so this is a coupling to be aware of rather than a proven stall. No test shows a worker-only deployment, with no queued PR label, still reaching merge.",
      "id": "required-checks-wait-completes-worker-job",
